{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Feast for the Dead: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja18'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 18 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Sīlavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ethics </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>8. Matakabhattajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Feast for the Dead: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Evañce sattā jāneyyuṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If beings only knew </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dukkhāyaṁ jātisambhavo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>how this suffering is created by birth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na pāṇo pāṇinaṁ haññe, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>no creature would kill another, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pāṇaghātī hi socatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for the slayer of creatures grieves. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Matakabhattajātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
